Subject: [PATCH] Cancel the initial native model load when rendering exits

Applies after mujoco_ros2_control-0.1.2-ui-thread-cleanup.patch

MuJoCo 3.12 Simulate::Load waits only for loadrequest == 0. If rendering
exits during startup, it can leave the physics thread waiting forever
while shutdown joins it

Use the same public load handshake with exitrequest as an additional
cancellation predicate. Serialize the request and exit check under the
simulation mutex, and notify its waiters on the UI thread when rendering
has stopped. Do not time out successful model loads or advance physics
until loading has actually completed

--- a/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
+++ b/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
@@ -625,6 +625,12 @@
       // Blocks until terminated
       RCLCPP_INFO(get_logger(), "Starting the MuJoCo rendering thread...");
       sim_->RenderLoop();
+
+      // A model load may still be waiting when rendering exits during startup.
+      {
+        const std::unique_lock<std::recursive_mutex> lock(sim_->mtx);
+        sim_->cond_loadrequest.notify_all();
+      }
 
       // Destroy GL resources on the thread that owns the current context,
       // before it exits or ROS shutdown lets another thread destroy sim_.
@@ -811,7 +817,23 @@
     }
     else
     {
-      sim_->Load(mj_model_, mj_data_, model_path_.c_str());
+      // Use Simulate's load handshake, including cancellation if rendering exits.
+      std::unique_lock<std::recursive_mutex> lock(*sim_mutex_);
+      if (sim_->exitrequest.load())
+      {
+        return;
+      }
+      sim_->mnew_ = mj_model_;
+      sim_->dnew_ = mj_data_;
+      mju::strcpy_arr(sim_->filename, model_path_.c_str());
+      sim_->loadrequest = 2;
+      sim_->cond_loadrequest.wait(lock, [this]() {
+        return sim_->loadrequest == 0 || sim_->exitrequest.load();
+      });
+      if (sim_->exitrequest.load())
+      {
+        return;
+      }
     }
     // lock the sim mutex
     {
